.TH EXTRACT-FEMACROS.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
extract\-femacros.py \- build the otsdaq FE macro inventory from source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/extract\-femacros.py
.RB [ \-r
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE | \- ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR GLOB ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans every
.B registerFEMacroFunction(
call in files ending
.IR .cc ,
.IR .h ,
.I .hh
or
.I .cpp
under the checkouts matching
.I GLOB
and writes a JSON inventory of the FE macros they register: name, handler,
input and output argument names, permission, allowed callers and description,
with the source file and line of each call.
.PP
Calls span many lines and are interleaved with comments, so the scanner
matches parentheses rather than lines.
A call inside a
.B /* */
block, or on a line containing
.B //
before it, is recorded with
.BR "active: false" .
Calls in files whose name contains
.B otsdaq_import_tracker_test_stand
emit registration source rather than register anything; they are recorded with
.B "generator: true"
and left out of the summary's totals.
.PP
This is a repository-maintenance tool and is not installed.
Run it after updating the otsdaq submodules to refresh
.IR data/otsdaq\-femacros.json ,
which backs
.IR doc/otsdaq\-command\-surface.md .
.PP
The result is what the source registers, not what a live system exposes: the
DTC front end re-registers its child ROCs' macros at configure time.
.B "mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq macros"
reads the live list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory holding the checkouts.
Default: two levels above
.IR tools/ ,
which for a submodule checkout is the
.B mu2edaq\-main
superproject.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Output file; parent directories are created.
Default:
.I data/otsdaq\-femacros.json
in this checkout.
.B \-
writes the JSON to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pattern " \fIGLOB\fR"
Checkout glob under
.IR DIR .
Default:
.BR otsdaq\-mu2e* .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not print the "wrote" line or the summary.
Without
.BR \-q ,
the summary is printed to standard output even with
.BR "\-o \-" ,
after the JSON.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON array, one object per call:
.PP
.RS
.nf
package, file, line   where it was found
active                false if commented out
generator             true if the file only emits registration source
name                  the macro name as callers must spell it
handler               the C++ method it dispatches to
inputs, outputs       argument names, exactly as registered
permission            requiredUserPermissions, as source text
callers               allowedCallingFEs
description           the help text, when one was given
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/otsdaq\-femacros.json
Default output, tracked in git.
.TP
.I doc/otsdaq\-command\-surface.md
The survey this inventory supports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.I DIR
does not exist or contains nothing matching
.IR GLOB .
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Refresh the tracked inventory and print the summary:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./tools/extract\-femacros.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./tools/extract\-femacros.py \-o \- \-q | jq '.[] | select(.active) | .name'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-otsdaq (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
